{
  "id": "ep105",
  "duration": 57.165,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.072,
      "text": "A single storm on Saturn can wrap around the entire planet.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn Storm December 2010.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech/SSI",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_Storm_December_2010.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.072,
      "end": 11.417,
      "text": "Jupiter is thought to lack planet-encircling storms, but Saturn periodically erupts with colossal Great White Spots.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Jupiter - Perijove 18 - GRS Map Projected (48062525062).jpg",
        "credit": "Kevin M. Gill",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jupiter_-_Perijove_18_-_GRS_Map_Projected_(48062525062).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.067,
          "end": 7.733,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.733,
          "end": 11.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.417,
      "end": 18.312,
      "text": "Six of these megastorms have emerged since 1876, returning roughly every twenty to thirty years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Professor Asaph Hall.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Professor_Asaph_Hall.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.433,
          "end": 14.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 14.867,
          "end": 18.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.312,
      "end": 24.557,
      "text": "In late 2010, NASA's Cassini spacecraft watched a storm head grow to the size of Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn Storm Panoramas.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech/SSI",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_Storm_Panoramas.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 20.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 20.867,
          "end": 24.567,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.557,
      "end": 30.427,
      "text": "The tempest generated up to ten lightning flashes per second while whipping out a massive tail.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.567,
          "end": 30.433,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.427,
      "end": 36.552,
      "text": "Within six months, that tail wrapped entirely around Saturn until it caught up with itself.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn - August 18 2011 (30526489196).jpg",
        "credit": "Kevin Gill from Los Angeles, CA, United States",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_-_August_18_2011_(30526489196).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.433,
          "end": 36.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.552,
      "end": 44.647,
      "text": "Caltech scientists discovered heavy water vapor suppresses atmospheric convection for decades until cooling overrides it.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Athenauem Caltech 1975.png",
        "credit": "Unknown authorUnknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Athenauem_Caltech_1975.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.567,
          "end": 44.633,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 44.647,
      "end": 51.097,
      "text": "Chemical remnants from these violent eruptions actually linger in Saturn's skies for centuries.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Very Large Array -- New Mexico, U.S.A. -- 2009-08.jpg",
        "credit": "CGP Grey",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Very_Large_Array_--_New_Mexico,_U.S.A._--_2009-08.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 44.633,
          "end": 47.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 47.867,
          "end": 51.1,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 51.097,
      "end": 56.815,
      "text": "Those deep atmospheric scars remain until Saturn unleashes its next planetary monster.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn Storm December 2010.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech/SSI",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_Storm_December_2010.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 51.1,
          "end": 57.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
